{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbaeQeRbrCqR5ncV9Q1i", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Flags in this project are plain booleans in a TOML file, read through one helper.\n\n**How it works**\n- **Declaration:** `flags.toml` at the repo root has a `[flags]` table of `name = true|false`. Right now it only contains `invoice-pdf-v2 = false`.\n- **Reading:** `flags.is_on(\"name\")` in `src/flags.py:7` returns `bool(_FLAGS.get(name, False))`. A flag that isn't declared reads as off.\n- **Loading:** the TOML file is read once, when `src/flags.py` is imported. Changing a flag means editing the file and restarting.\n- **Listing:** `flags.all_flags()` returns a copy of the whole table.\n\nThe convention (stored in EngramDB, and it matches the code) is to read flags only through `is_on`. Flag names are kebab-case and must be declared in `flags.toml`.\n\n**For your checkout flow**\n1. Add `new-checkout = false` to `flags.toml`. The name is just a suggestion.\n2. At the branch point, write `if flags.is_on(\"new-checkout\"): ...new flow... else: ...existing flow...`.\n3. Turn it on by setting it to `true`.\n\nThere's no per-user, percentage or environment targeting. A flag is on or off for everyone. If you need a gradual rollout, that would have to be built.\n\nI haven't found where checkout lives or added anything yet. Tell me where the flow is and I can wire it in."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 160, "cache_read_input_tokens": 21787, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 160}, "output_tokens": 480, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "134e7a18-6b10-4b67-81a5-7eefbc5f6e28", "uuid": "a143